00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:17.180
scaling remain the ones to track. From an engineering standpoint, placing semiconductor

00:05:17.180 --> 00:05:23.360
test hardware on an operational Falcon 9 booster subjects the chips to the full stack of launch

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:28.760
environments in a single flight. The booster experiences peak dynamic pressure, sustained

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:34.820
acceleration and rapid thermal gradients. Any test article must survive these without dedicated

00:05:34.820 --> 00:05:40.260
vibration tables or thermal chambers. This approach collapses the cost of environmental

00:05:40.260 --> 00:05:45.680
qualification from a standalone campaign down to marginal mass and integration effort on an

00:05:45.680 --> 00:05:52.520
already scheduled mission. Data returned after recovery can directly compare pre-flight and post-flight

00:05:52.520 --> 00:05:58.320
electrical performance, revealing whether packaging or interconnects shift under real loads.

00:05:58.900 --> 00:06:04.780
If yields remain high, the same method scales to future orbital compute payloads that must tolerate

00:06:04.780 --> 00:06:09.800
